            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for immortal, then the Hindi for to swallow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तपस्या",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तपस्या — tapasyā — \"penance; austerity\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ऋषि ने जंगल में बारह साल तपस्या की। ṛṣi ne jaṅgal meṁ bārah sāl tapasyā kī. The sage did penance in the forest for twelve years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तपस्या (tapasyā) is Sanskrit tapasyā (Monier-Williams), from tapas, heat and then the hard discipline of a holy life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
