              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कोसना — kosnā — \"to curse; to rail at\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बूढ़ी औरत चोर को कोस रही थी। būṛhī aurat cor ko kos rahī thī. The old woman was cursing the thief."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने चोर को कोसा, usne cor ko kosā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कोसना (kosnā) goes back to Sanskrit krośati, \"cries out\" (CDIAL 3612). It is everyday cursing in words, not a sage's शाप (śāp)."
            }
          ]
        },
